  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Waste management and Bioeconomy workshops at the Circular Economy Week in Lagos</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity supports the organisation of Circular Economy Week in Lagos in February 2026, by the Netherlands consulate-general in Lagos and the Netherlands Enterprise Agency (RVO).The week will bring together government, business, knowledge institutes and non-governmental organisations (NGOs) to develop a locally supported circular economy and waste action plan.The programme focuses on access to finance, waste management and the bioeconomy, including the launch of a new circular economy fund for Nigerian start ups and small- and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs). It will feature six thematic workshops, three on waste management and three on the bioeconomy, with participation from selected Dutch circular economy experts and companies.The initiative also supports policy dialogue, fosters partnerships between Dutch and Nigerian stakeholders and documents key results and lessons learned to guide future collaboration.</narrative>
  </description>
